{"engine":"Windows.Media.Ocr en-US","scale":3,"pages":[{"page":1,"width":2448,"height":3168,"lines":[{"text":"OF","x":418,"y":265,"w":41,"h":27},{"text":"RECEIVED","x":1233,"y":191,"w":382,"h":72},{"text":"OFFICE OF","x":661,"y":291,"w":230,"h":35},{"text":"MARK CHURCH","x":1649,"y":340,"w":343,"h":41},{"text":"ASSESSOR-COUNTY CLERK-AIJG 1 1","x":660,"y":350,"w":790,"h":59},{"text":"CHIEF ELECTIONS OFFICER &","x":1590,"y":396,"w":462,"h":32},{"text":"RECORDER & ELECTIONS","x":661,"y":418,"w":557,"h":44},{"text":"ASSESSOR-COUNTY CLERK-RECORDER","x":1520,"y":439,"w":605,"h":33},{"text":"COUNTY OF SAN MATEOCity of Menlo Park","x":660,"y":489,"w":1026,"h":63},{"text":"Ballot Measure Primary Form","x":618,"y":590,"w":1235,"h":47},{"text":"A ballot argument will not be accepted unless accompanied by this completed typed form, which shall contain the","x":305,"y":642,"w":1790,"h":36},{"text":"printed name(s) and signature(s) of the person(s) submitting it or, if submitted on behalf of a bona fide association of","x":308,"y":683,"w":1834,"h":37},{"text":"citizens, the name of the association and the printed name and signature of at least one of its principal officers.","x":307,"y":725,"w":1741,"h":36},{"text":"Please make sure you are using proper format before submitting to the Elections Office.","x":308,"y":766,"w":1488,"h":35},{"text":"Word count limit for Primary Arguments = 300 words","x":306,"y":821,"w":825,"h":36},{"text":"Ballot Measure","x":308,"y":877,"w":232,"h":28},{"text":"Primary Argument in Favor of","x":364,"y":939,"w":468,"h":36},{"text":"for the General Election","x":845,"y":871,"w":376,"h":34},{"text":"to be held on November 3, 2026","x":1456,"y":871,"w":511,"h":34},{"text":"Primary Argument Against","x":1104,"y":939,"w":416,"h":35},{"text":"This argument is submitted by (check ONLY ONE):","x":806,"y":1004,"w":857,"h":35},{"text":"The County of San Mateo Board of Supervisors or the Governing Body of a School District or Special","x":430,"y":1056,"w":1714,"h":37},{"text":"District","x":432,"y":1097,"w":121,"h":28},{"text":"Name of Governing Body:","x":432,"y":1139,"w":408,"h":35},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":431,"y":1225,"w":507,"h":29},{"text":"Phone:","x":431,"y":1309,"w":110,"h":28},{"text":"Email:","x":1313,"y":1310,"w":95,"h":27},{"text":"Member(s) of the County of San Mateo Board of Supervisors or the Governing Body of a School","x":432,"y":1397,"w":1619,"h":35},{"text":"District or S ecial District","x":432,"y":1437,"w":436,"h":28},{"text":"Name of Governing Body:","x":432,"y":1480,"w":408,"h":35},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":431,"y":1564,"w":508,"h":29},{"text":"Phone:","x":432,"y":1648,"w":108,"h":28},{"text":"Bona Fide Association of Citizens","x":432,"y":1736,"w":573,"h":28},{"text":"Email:","x":1312,"y":1648,"w":96,"h":27},{"text":"If this argument is filed by a bona fide association of citizens, the signers of the argument must be affiliated","x":433,"y":1776,"w":1678,"h":36},{"text":"with the association and be authorized to sign the argument on its behalf. Provide the printed name and","x":431,"y":1817,"w":1640,"h":35},{"text":"signature of at least one rinci al officer of the association.","x":431,"y":1858,"w":928,"h":34},{"text":"Name of Association:","x":432,"y":1901,"w":335,"h":29},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":432,"y":1986,"w":507,"h":29},{"text":"Phone:","x":433,"y":2070,"w":109,"h":27},{"text":"Individual Voters Eligible to Vote on the Measure","x":433,"y":2157,"w":824,"h":35},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":433,"y":2209,"w":507,"h":29},{"text":"Alex Beltramo","x":437,"y":2250,"w":221,"h":27},{"text":"Combination of Voters and Associations","x":433,"y":2381,"w":686,"h":28},{"text":"Contact Person's Printed Name:","x":433,"y":2434,"w":508,"h":28},{"text":"phone:","x":435,"y":2518,"w":108,"h":28},{"text":"Email:","x":1312,"y":2070,"w":96,"h":27},{"text":"Email:","x":1314,"y":2518,"w":96,"h":28},{"text":"Arguments will be emailed to the contact person listed here for review before they are printed in the Sample","x":326,"y":2601,"w":1829,"h":35},{"text":"Ballot & Official Voter Information Pamphlets.","x":854,"y":2642,"w":768,"h":35},{"text":"Please complete the reverse side of this form.","x":853,"y":2687,"w":771,"h":33},{"text":"40 Tower Road, San Mateo, CA 94402","x":905,"y":2730,"w":666,"h":37},{"text":"P 650.312.5222 F 650.312.5348 email registrar@smcacre.gov web www.smcacre.gov","x":471,"y":2778,"w":1537,"h":38}]},{"page":2,"width":2448,"height":3168,"lines":[{"text":"ARGUMENT IN FAVOR OF MEASURE","x":799,"y":457,"w":771,"h":39},{"text":"Vote YES! on Measure _ to give voters a say before the City Council can","x":310,"y":617,"w":1582,"h":51},{"text":"permanently convert downtown parking plazas into high-rise developments.","x":313,"y":681,"w":1624,"h":48},{"text":"A FLAWED PLAN","x":310,"y":801,"w":352,"h":37},{"text":"Over 3,000 Menlo Park residents signed the Measure X petition because they don't","x":312,"y":861,"w":1761,"h":52},{"text":"believe Council's plan is an effective way to provide the low-income housing we","x":312,"y":923,"w":1701,"h":52},{"text":"need.","x":311,"y":985,"w":117,"h":34},{"text":"Council presumed that developers, who'd get the plazas for $1 [year, could pay to","x":310,"y":1105,"w":1738,"h":53},{"text":"replace 556 spaces. But the developer proposals tell a different story, and Menlo","x":310,"y":1167,"w":1723,"h":51},{"text":"Park could be on the hook for tens of millions to build public garages. Furthermore,","x":310,"y":1228,"w":1767,"h":52},{"text":"the City's done insufficient analysis on economic impact, traffic, parking,","x":307,"y":1289,"w":1562,"h":52},{"text":"overcrowded classrooms, or fire safety.","x":309,"y":1351,"w":847,"h":46},{"text":"Already, 135 downtown businesses publicly oppose the Council's plan, as they'd be","x":306,"y":1473,"w":1797,"h":52},{"text":"unlikely to survive years of high-rise construction followed by a permanent loss of","x":309,"y":1535,"w":1740,"h":51},{"text":"convenient parking.","x":308,"y":1596,"w":418,"h":45},{"text":"A SMARTER WAY FORWARD","x":305,"y":1718,"w":600,"h":36},{"text":"Most residents aren't aware, but Menlo Park is proving it can deliver housing without","x":308,"y":1778,"w":1796,"h":52},{"text":"this plan. Menlo Park's own July 2026 housing update reported that housing","x":305,"y":1839,"w":1615,"h":52},{"text":"capacity exceeds state requirements by 30%. Since 2010, Menlo Park has added","x":306,"y":1900,"w":1719,"h":48},{"text":"more than 1 ,400 homes, nearly 30% more growth than the county average.","x":308,"y":1962,"w":1588,"h":52},{"text":"And 1 , 750 more homes are on the way, near downtown, at the former SRI and USGS","x":303,"y":2084,"w":1792,"h":48},{"text":"sites. The problem is that not enough of them are affordable to local workers. We","x":306,"y":2145,"w":1726,"h":48},{"text":"can remedy that by incentivizing the developers to shift units to the very-low-","x":306,"y":2208,"w":1636,"h":50},{"text":"income category. The City's cost to do that would be far less than giving away public","x":306,"y":2267,"w":1795,"h":53},{"text":"land, building expensive garages, and undermining local businesses.","x":306,"y":2328,"w":1467,"h":48},{"text":"Menlo Park has many ways to meet its housing goals. The greatest risk is Council","x":306,"y":2450,"w":1723,"h":50},{"text":"pushing forward, without community consent, with a flawed, unfunded plan that","x":306,"y":2510,"w":1752,"h":52},{"text":"could fail us all.","x":306,"y":2572,"w":332,"h":36},{"text":"Vote YES! on Measure","x":302,"y":2694,"w":468,"h":38},{"text":"It ensures our voices are heard.","x":856,"y":2697,"w":670,"h":38}]},{"page":3,"width":2448,"height":3168,"lines":[{"text":"Primary Argument Signers Form","x":768,"y":289,"w":569,"h":36},{"text":"No more than five signatures shall appear with any argument. If more than five signatures","x":299,"y":345,"w":1471,"h":37},{"text":"are submitted, the first five listed shall be printed. Names and titles listed will be printed in","x":298,"y":388,"w":1467,"h":37},{"text":"the order that they are listed below. Place a checkmark in the author column if the signer is","x":297,"y":431,"w":1494,"h":37},{"text":"the author of the argument. A signer can only list one title. Honorifics such as M.D., Dr.,","x":297,"y":473,"w":1445,"h":38},{"text":"Esquire, etc. with a name are not accepted.","x":299,"y":516,"w":708,"h":37},{"text":"If the signers are part of a bona fide association, there is no requirement that they be","x":300,"y":582,"w":1379,"h":37},{"text":"eligible to vote on the measure. However, for each such signing individual, the title under","x":298,"y":624,"w":1460,"h":37},{"text":"the signer's name must list the name of that bona fide association and may include their","x":296,"y":666,"w":1437,"h":38},{"text":"position within that association.","x":298,"y":709,"w":507,"h":36},{"text":"By signing below, the undersigned state that they have read the argument and believe it not","x":299,"y":774,"w":1498,"h":38},{"text":"Author","x":1854,"y":291,"w":123,"h":28},{"text":"3","x":1907,"y":435,"w":23,"h":17},{"text":"Pronouns:","x":1844,"y":1126,"w":164,"h":30},{"text":"He/His:","x":1844,"y":1180,"w":118,"h":30},{"text":"She/Her.","x":1843,"y":1223,"w":142,"h":30},{"text":"They/Them:","x":1842,"y":1266,"w":195,"h":35},{"text":"Verified","x":2037,"y":290,"w":137,"h":30},{"text":"o","x":2099,"y":387,"w":21,"h":19},{"text":".7","x":158,"y":1696,"w":47,"h":45},{"text":"to be false or misleading.","x":297,"y":816,"w":410,"h":37},{"text":"Type information clearly.","x":297,"y":880,"w":406,"h":37},{"text":"1. Name:","x":304,"y":941,"w":177,"h":39},{"text":"Phone:","x":298,"y":1032,"w":111,"h":30},{"text":"Address:","x":295,"y":1125,"w":142,"h":29},{"text":"Signature","x":297,"y":1218,"w":155,"h":36},{"text":"X. Name:","x":282,"y":1309,"w":200,"h":46},{"text":"Signature-","x":297,"y":1591,"w":163,"h":36},{"text":"Name:","x":375,"y":1688